@startuml AssignmentFlow
actor Instructor
participant "Content Service" as CS
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "RabbitMQ" as RMQ
participant "Notification Service" as NT
actor Students

== Create Assignment ==
Instructor -> CS: POST /assignments\n{title, description, startDate, dueDate,\nskillIds, tutorialIds, languages, testCases}

CS -> CS: Validate dates (due > start)\nValidate skillIds and tutorialIds exist

CS -> DB: Save assignment as draft
DB --> CS: Assignment saved

CS --> Instructor: 201 Created + AssignmentResponse

== Publish Assignment ==
Instructor -> CS: PUT /assignments/{id}/publish

CS -> DB: Retrieve assignment
DB --> CS: Assignment details

CS -> CS: Check status == DRAFT\nCheck creatorId == userId

CS -> DB: Publish assignment
DB --> CS: Updated

CS -> RMQ: Publish AssignmentPublishedEvent\n{id, title, timestamp}

CS --> Instructor: 200 OK + AssignmentResponse

RMQ -> NT: Consume AssignmentPublishedEvent

NT -> Students: Send email/push notification\n"New assignment published: {title}"

@enduml
